# VerifAI Backend — example environment variables

Copy this file to `.env` and fill in real values. **Never commit the real `.env`** (it is git-ignored).

```bash
# Port the Express server listens on (default 3000)
PORT=3000

# PostgreSQL connection string
# Supabase: Project Settings -> Database -> Connection string (URI)
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:YOUR_PASSWORD@db.YOUR_PROJECT.supabase.co:5432/postgres

# Firebase Admin SDK service account
# Generate in Firebase Console -> Project Settings -> Service accounts
# Option A: path to the downloaded service-account JSON file
FIREBASE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_PATH=./firebase-service-account.json
# Option B: individual variables
FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=your-firebase-project-id
FIREBASE_CLIENT_EMAIL=firebase-adminsdk-xxxxx@your-firebase-project-id.iam.gserviceaccount.com
FIREBASE_PRIVATE_KEY="-----BEGIN PRIVATE KEY-----\nYOUR_KEY_HERE\n-----END PRIVATE KEY-----\n"

# Allowed origins for CORS (comma-separated)
CORS_ORIGIN=http://localhost:3000,http://localhost:5173
```
